@mislav 

> The NAME column is redundant because the value is entirely contained within REPO;

I originally had the first column as `NAME/OWNER` and it was _very_ hard to scan through. The output is jagged since NAMEs are of varying lengths. I also don't think people are mentally scanning first for names: they are going to notice a command name as potentially relevant to their interests as opposed to the identity of the author.

I then tried having the two columns "NAME OWNER" which is a better use of space, but doesn't give people a trivially copy-pastable argument to pass to `gh repo view` which felt like a papercut.

Ultimately nothing really felt right, but I think you are correct that width is too precious a commodity here. I'll just accept the jagged column on the left side and return to NAME/OWNER.

